# =============================================================================
# .env.test — the throwaway admin credential for the e2e / test stacks
# =============================================================================
#
# NOT FOR DEPLOYMENT. Everything in this file exists to let a stack that is
# created and destroyed by one test run log into itself. A real deployment sets
# ADMIN_PASSWORD (or INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD_FILE) from its own secret store;
# see the credential notes in the root docker-compose.yml.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL (#3490, #3938)
# Every e2e compose file and about forty e2e scripts need the same password, or
# the stack and the scripts cannot log into each other. Spelling a default into
# each of them put ~60 copies of one string in the repository, which is
# indistinguishable from a leaked credential to a secret scanner. The value is
# written here, once, and referenced everywhere else with no inline default.
#
# HOW IT IS READ
# The syntax below is deliberately the subset that is BOTH a dotenv file and a
# POSIX shell script, so one file serves both consumers with identical
# semantics:
#   * `docker compose` reads it through each e2e service's `env_file:`, which
#     is relative to the compose file, so no `--env-file` flag and no change to
#     any existing invocation is needed;
#   * host-side scripts `.`-source it via scripts/lib/test-env.sh.
#
# OVERRIDING
# `:-` means an exported value always wins, in both paths. To give a run a
# credential that exists nowhere in this repository:
#   export AK_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD="$(openssl rand -base64 24)"
# scripts/run-e2e-tests.sh does exactly that on your behalf.
# =============================================================================
export AK_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD=${AK_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD:-ak-e2e-throwaway-not-for-deployment}

# The two names the backend and the test scripts actually read. Both default to
# the one value above, and both still honour an explicit override of their own.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=${ADMIN_PASSWORD:-$AK_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}
ADMIN_PASS=${ADMIN_PASS:-$AK_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}
